Bill Green wrote:
> So I stupidly trapped a monster between a boulder and a pit.
> After expending my supply of daggers without killing it, I 
> was headed back downstairs to try to find some other way to dispatch 
> whatever it was. 

Okay, so far so good; still choices. Get a heap of rocks and throw
them past the boulder until the critter dies. The same is possible
with wands, say, of magic missile.

There's the possibility to strip naked and drop (quite) everything,
then you may squeeze onto the boulder square; but that will provide
you a luck penalty.

> Of course, something (I think it was a Gnome Lord)
> had found the scrolls of earth I left on the first Sokoban level;

Bad. In the first place, don't ever leave scrolls behind that will
be used by monsters; a scroll of earth is such a scroll. Deposit it
beneath a boulder or at the stairs that lead to Sokoban if you don't
want to carry the scroll with you.

> they
> fell in such a way that they're all immovable.  And of course I didn't
> bring a pick-axe (I suppose this will teach me /that/ lesson).  

Now, getting rid of many boulders will drop your luck a lot. In case
you don't mind (I think I would) you can smash the boulders (pickaxe,
striking, force bolt), squeeze in between (as described above; but
that might just multiply your luck problem), or teleport away a row
of boulders.

> 
> Am I missing something obvious?  Or am I stuck for good? 

By stuck you mean that you cannot proceed in that optional branch?
You can, as depicted above, but it's costly.

> I know
> your god will teleport you to safety if you're confined to one 
> space by boulders, but I don't think that applies here, as I 
> still have access to the upstairs from Sokoban level 1.

